<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Kangaba</h1><p class="st-meta">1050 CE – 1235 CE (approx.) · capital Kangaba</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The small Mandinka kingdom on the upper Niger from which Sundiata Keita built the Mali Empire.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kangaba">Kangaba</a> was one of several <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandinka">Malinke</a> chiefdoms of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manding">Manden</a>, the upland country along the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> near today's border of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea">Guinea</a>. By the 11th century the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keita-dynasty">Keita clan</a> ruled there, and it lay within the orbit of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ghana-empire">Ghana Empire</a>, supplying gold from the nearby <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bure">Bure</a> fields.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its kings were hunters' and warriors' chiefs with a council of clan heads, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/griots">griots</a> kept their genealogies. Tradition names <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maghan-kon-fatta">Maghan Kon Fatta</a> as the father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sundiata-keita">Sundiata</a>. In the early 13th century the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manding">Manden</a> fell under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sosso-kingdom">Sosso kingdom</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumanguru-kante">Sumanguru Kante</a>, who killed or scattered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keita-dynasty">Keita</a> princes.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sundiata-keita">Sundiata Keita</a> returned from exile, united the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mande-peoples">Mande</a> clans and defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumanguru-kante">Sumanguru</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kirina">Kirina</a> around 1235, founding the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mali-empire">Mali Empire</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kangaba">Kangaba</a> remained the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keita-dynasty">Keita</a> heartland, and its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamabolon">Kamabolon</a> sanctuary is still re-roofed every seven years in a ceremony recognised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco">UNESCO</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1050 CE – 1235 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">West Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:80.60%;width:3.68%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1050 CE – 1235 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kangaba</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Maghan Kon Fatta, Sundiata Keita</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Mande traditional religion and Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Maninka</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mali">Mali</a>, <a href="/countries/guinea">Guinea</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kangaba, Manden, Kaba</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1142&amp;focus=kingdom-of-kangaba" aria-label="Kingdom of Kangaba on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4449 1733 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Kangaba lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4769 1989L4782 1851M4769 1989L4769 1989"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4782 1851h0M4769 1989h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4769 1989h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4769 1989h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kangaba. <a href="/atlas?year=1142&amp;focus=kingdom-of-kangaba">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
